# Redirect rules live in netlify.toml, which Netlify validates at build time.
# Keeping them in one place avoids the precedence trap: rules in netlify.toml
# are processed BEFORE the ones in this file, so split rules mean the file you
# are reading may not be the one that wins.
#
# There is deliberately no `/*  /index.html  200` catch-all anywhere: that
# served the homepage with a 200 for every non-existent URL (a soft 404).
